From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dodaskot <pessdres@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 22:17:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 070/131] arm64: dts: a22x: physical panel size for simpledrm

Without it simpledrm reports 285x637 mm (96 dpi) and size-aware clients
such as the Phosh on-screen keyboard draw far too small. Values from the
stock panel driver (68.43 x 152.57 mm).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts
index 0c2280c5a..bfc098cbf 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts
@@ -51,9 +51,19 @@ framebuffer@7c9b0000 {
 			stride = <(1088 * 4)>;
 			format = "a8r8g8b8";
 			backlight = <&backlight>;
+			panel = <&fb_panel>;
 		};
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Physical size for simpledrm (else it assumes 96 dpi and the on-screen
+	 * keyboard gets far too thin): 68.43 x 152.57 mm in the stock panel driver.
+	 */
+	fb_panel: simplefb-panel {
+		width-mm = <68>;
+		height-mm = <152>;
+	};
+
 	pio_ml: pinctrl@10005000 {
 		compatible = "mediatek,mt6833-pinctrl";
 		reg = <0 0x10005000 0 0x1000>,
